[3b] Regression diagnostics (linearity, homoscedasticity, normality)...
  --- Regression diagnostics (autosomal training genes, Human skeletal muscle (ribonn)) ---
  Normality of TE (actual, log2 scale, n=4,650): skew = -0.235, excess kurtosis = -0.141, D'Agostino K^2 p = 9.4e-11, Jarque-Bera p = 7.01e-11
  Normality of residuals: skew = -0.333, excess kurtosis = -0.050, D'Agostino K^2 p = 1.31e-18, Jarque-Bera p = 1.65e-19
  Homoscedasticity (Breusch-Pagan): LM stat = 91.913, p = 0.00642
  Linearity (Ramsey RESET, power=3 on fitted values): F = 0.370, p = 0.691
  (in each test, p < 0.05 => reject the null of normality / homoscedasticity / linearity)
